1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,696
First of all I'd just like to say, Cristina and Ibrahim,

2
00:00:04,696 --> 00:00:09,733
that I really enjoyed watching your video about student life last week,

3
00:00:09,733 --> 00:00:11,760
and I could see that the rest of the group did too.

4
00:00:11,760 --> 00:00:13,417
You did really well,

5
00:00:13,417 --> 00:00:15,660
and I hope that you got a lot out of it.

6
00:00:15,660 --> 00:00:20,890
I'd like to use this tutorial as a feedback session, where you reflect on

7
00:00:20,890 --> 00:00:22,640
the experience of doing the project.

8
00:00:22,640 --> 00:00:29,590
So Cristina, I was wondering, what did you enjoy most about making the video?

9
00:00:29,590 --> 00:00:32,310
I liked using the camera.

10
00:00:32,310 --> 00:00:35,000
Is it the first time you've operated one like that?

11
00:00:35,000 --> 00:00:36,190
Yes, it is.

12
00:00:36,190 --> 00:00:37,807
Well the results were very good!

13
00:00:37,807 --> 00:00:39,100
Anything else?

14
00:00:39,100 --> 00:00:43,454
I also enjoyed visiting one of the British students we filmed.

15
00:00:43,454 --> 00:00:46,620
I'd never been inside a British home before.

16
00:00:46,620 --> 00:00:47,836
OK Cristina, thanks.

17
00:00:47,836 --> 00:00:49,458
What about you, Ibrahim?

18
00:00:49,458 --> 00:00:51,080
What did you enjoy?

19
00:00:51,080 --> 00:00:54,809
Well for me it was a very good chance to get to know students

20
00:00:54,809 --> 00:00:56,140
who are on other courses,

21
00:00:56,140 --> 00:00:58,271
because everyone in our group is studying English,

22
00:00:58,271 --> 00:01:02,000
and we don't usually have much to do with the rest of the college.

23
00:01:02,000 --> 00:01:02,790
Yes, good.

24
00:01:02,790 --> 00:01:05,950
Do you think you'll maintain the contact now?

25
00:01:05,950 --> 00:01:06,678
I hope so.

26
00:01:06,678 --> 00:01:09,590
I've invited three of them to have dinner with me next week.

27
00:01:09,590 --> 00:01:09,923
Great!

28
00:01:09,923 --> 00:01:14,584
If you haven't decided what to make yet I can tell you they'll love

29
00:01:14,584 --> 00:01:15,583
trying Arab dishes.

30
00:01:15,583 --> 00:01:18,580
And of course, it's good for your English too.

31
00:01:18,580 --> 00:01:20,156
Cristina, what did you find?

32
00:01:20,156 --> 00:01:24,569
What was the most useful aspect of the project from the point of view

33
00:01:24,569 --> 00:01:25,830
of the English practice?

34
00:01:25,830 --> 00:01:26,540
I think,

35
00:01:26,540 --> 00:01:31,510
when we were being shown how to edit the film, we had to follow

36
00:01:31,510 --> 00:01:32,220
the instructions.

37
00:01:32,220 --> 00:01:35,060
And that was very good practice for me.

38
00:01:35,060 --> 00:01:39,320
And I also learned some technical words that I hadn't heard before.

39
00:01:39,320 --> 00:01:40,753
What about you Ibrahim?

40
00:01:40,753 --> 00:01:43,620
What was the most useful for your English?

41
00:01:43,620 --> 00:01:45,664
It was listening to the British students,

42
00:01:45,664 --> 00:01:49,753
because they don't speak as slowly as most of the tutors on our course.

43
00:01:49,753 --> 00:01:51,797
I think they speak at natural speed,

44
00:01:51,797 --> 00:01:54,426
so it forces me to get used to it.

45
00:01:54,426 --> 00:01:56,470
And they use a lot of slang.

46
00:01:56,470 --> 00:01:59,300
So you learned some new words which will be useful?

47
00:01:59,300 --> 00:02:00,070
Yes.

48
00:02:00,070 --> 00:02:00,472
Good.

49
00:02:00,472 --> 00:02:02,079
I'm glad it helped.

50
00:02:02,079 --> 00:02:05,294
Well, we've talked a little bit about enjoyment,

51
00:02:05,294 --> 00:02:06,901
and about language practice.

52
00:02:06,901 --> 00:02:08,911
Were there any other benefits?

53
00:02:08,911 --> 00:02:12,929
What else did you feel you'd learnt from the project?

54
00:02:12,929 --> 00:02:15,340
Was it useful in other ways?

55
00:02:15,340 --> 00:02:19,638
Yes, well firstly, I learned how to use a video camera.

56
00:02:19,638 --> 00:02:25,109
And also, I think I really learned a lot about working together with other

57
00:02:25,109 --> 00:02:25,500
people.

58
00:02:25,500 --> 00:02:29,384
I've never done anything with a group before,

59
00:02:29,384 --> 00:02:33,754
and we had to find ways of cooperating, erm,

60
00:02:33,754 --> 00:02:34,725
and compromising,

61
00:02:34,725 --> 00:02:36,667
and sometimes persuading people,

62
00:02:36,667 --> 00:02:39,580
when they don't agree with you.

63
00:02:39,580 --> 00:02:39,943
Yes,

64
00:02:39,943 --> 00:02:42,850
that is a very useful experience, I know.

65
00:02:42,850 --> 00:02:44,750
What about you, Ibrahim?

66
00:02:44,750 --> 00:02:48,169
Well, I think I learnt a lot about how important editing is.

67
00:02:48,169 --> 00:02:51,302
When you're filming you think that everything's going to be interesting,

68
00:02:51,302 --> 00:02:54,721
but in fact we cut around half of it in the end,

69
00:02:54,721 --> 00:02:56,430
and then it was much better.

70
00:02:56,430 --> 00:02:56,786
Good.

71
00:02:56,786 --> 00:02:59,634
Well, one last thing I'd like to ask.

72
00:02:59,634 --> 00:03:03,907
What mistakes do you think you, as a group that is, made?

73
00:03:03,907 --> 00:03:08,892
I mean, to put it another way, if you had to do it all

74
00:03:08,892 --> 00:03:11,740
over again, is there anything you'd do differently?

75
00:03:11,740 --> 00:03:13,624
We didn't plan very well.

76
00:03:13,624 --> 00:03:18,900
For example, we didn't decide on dates when we'd complete each separate step of

77
00:03:18,900 --> 00:03:19,654
the project,

78
00:03:19,654 --> 00:03:23,422
and we should have agreed about that in the beginning,

79
00:03:23,422 --> 00:03:26,060
because we were always late with everything!

80
00:03:26,060 --> 00:03:26,643
Right.

81
00:03:26,643 --> 00:03:27,810
Anything else?

82
00:03:27,810 --> 00:03:32,235
I think we should have tried to experiment more with the camera.

83
00:03:32,235 --> 00:03:33,710
I mean with angles,

84
00:03:33,710 --> 00:03:36,660
and the focus and that kind of thing.

85
00:03:36,660 --> 00:03:38,760
So you should have been more ambitious?

86
00:03:38,760 --> 00:03:39,960
Do you agree, Ibrahim?

87
00:03:39,960 --> 00:03:40,595
Not really.

88
00:03:40,595 --> 00:03:43,137
In fact, I think we were too ambitious.

89
00:03:43,137 --> 00:03:44,090
We were inexperienced,

90
00:03:44,090 --> 00:03:46,632
and we didn't have a lot of time,

91
00:03:46,632 --> 00:03:50,444
and we tried to do too much, to make a long film.

92
00:03:50,444 --> 00:03:54,892
Next time I would make a shorter one and try to get the quality

93
00:03:54,892 --> 00:03:55,210
better.

94
00:03:55,210 --> 00:03:55,625
Well,

95
00:03:55,625 --> 00:03:56,868
that's very interesting.

96
00:03:56,868 --> 00:04:02,673
Next semester we will be doing another video project-with a different content, of course-but

97
00:04:02,673 --> 00:04:08,062
you'll have an opportunity to put into practice what you've learnt this time.

98
00:04:08,062 --> 00:04:10,550
Do you have any ideas about...
